      "title": "NASA identifies potential biosignature in Mars rock sample",
      "content_html": "Researchers are investigating Mars, Jupiter’s icy moons and other solar-system sites as possible habitats, but Earth remains the only world known to support life. NASA’s Perseverance rover collected a rock sample in July 2024 that the agency later described as containing a potential biosignature: organic material and mineral patterns that could reflect microbial activity but also have possible nonbiological explanations.\n\nMars preserves evidence of ancient surface water, while Europa and Enceladus may hold oceans beneath ice. Habitable conditions do not establish that organisms exist; water, usable energy and accessible chemical ingredients must come together over time. NASA’s Europa Clipper and the European Space Agency’s JUICE mission are traveling to study Jupiter’s icy moons, where possible exchanges between surface and subsurface reservoirs also raise planetary-protection concerns.",
