      "title": "Russia lets renewable power projects delay commissioning by another two years",
      "content_html": "Russia has allowed eligible renewable-energy projects supplying the retail electricity market to postpone commissioning by a further 24 months from their previously revised dates. Project participants or their legal successors must apply by Dec. 31, 2026. Deadline changes require approval from a government commission on electricity development, and investors face no penalty for approved delays or cancellations.\n\nThe government adopted Resolution No. 1496 on Nov. 12, published it the next day and scheduled it to take effect Nov. 21. The government had previously permitted a one-time extension for renewable projects on the wholesale market.",
