      "id": "https://www.archdaily.com/1188504/jswd-wins-competition-to-design-mixed-use-riymar-towers-in-riyadh-saudi-arabia",
      "url": "https://www.archdaily.com/1188504/jswd-wins-competition-to-design-mixed-use-riymar-towers-in-riyadh-saudi-arabia",
      "title": "JSWD Wins Competition to Design Mixed-Use RIYMAR Towers in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia",
      "content_html": "<p>German architecture practice <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/office/jswd-architekten\">JSWD</a> has been selected to design RIYMAR <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/tag/towers\">Towers</a>, a proposed mixed-use development in <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/tag/riyadh/page/1\">Riyadh</a>, <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/country/saudi-arabia/page/1\">Saudi Arabia</a>, following an international invited architecture competition organized by <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/tag/malcolm-reading-consultants\">Malcolm Reading Consultants</a> on behalf of RIYMAR Real Estate. Located near the intersection of King Fahd Road and Olaya Street, adjacent to the Riyadh Gallery complex, the project is planned as a new development combining residential, hospitality, office, retail, and leisure functions. The project is positioned within the broader urban transformation outlined by <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/tag/vision-2030\">Saudi Arabia's Vision 2030</a>, which includes objectives related to tourism, cultural development, hospitality, and increased homeownership.</p>",
